{title: Tower to the Heavens}
{subtitle: Genesis 11:1–9}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×17

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They baked the bricks and they burned them hard
They mixed the tar in the city yard
One people with one language, one dream in every eye
We'll build ourselves a tower that will scrape against the sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Come, let [F#]us build ourselves a city
[C#]With a tower [G#]that reaches to the heavens [D#m]
And make [F#]a name for our[C#]selves
Make [G#]a name, make a name for [D#m]ourselves
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Higher went the scaffolding, higher went the pride
Nothing we set our minds to could be denied
But the LORD came down to see the city and the tower
That the children of man were building in their hour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Come, let [F#]us build ourselves a city
[C#]With a tower [G#]that reaches to the heavens [D#m]
And make a [F#]name for our[C#]selves
Make a [G#]name, make a name for our[D#m]selves
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] | [G#] | ×4

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Then the [D#m]words began to tan[F#]gle and the [C#]voices turned to [G#]noise
The [D#m]foreman couldn't call [F#]them and the buil[C#]ders lost their [G#]poise
So the [D#m]LORD scattered them from there [F#]over the face [C#]of the whole [G#]earth
And [D#m]they [F#]stopped [C#]building the c[G#]ity
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
A name for our[D#m]selves
It was never ours to [F#]make
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [C#] | [G#] | [D#m] | [F#] | ×3
| [C#] | [G#] | [D#m] |
